out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Rizk has stated eight conditions this year and six produced reapplications, and five of the six were refused again, and in four of the five the condition she had stated was one the applicant could manufacture, such as if the evidence of ownership were stronger, which is an instruction to go and get three more letters, and three more letters arrived. Mrs Khoury said and you refused them, and she refused them because the ownership evidence had never been the reason: she had stated a condition about the application and the reason was a condition about the district, and the applicant did exactly what her sentence told them to do. Mr Attar asked which conditions are safe to state, and Mrs Khoury said the ones the applicant cannot manufacture, and the test is that simple, because the district rule is applied at the date of the committee is a fact about a rule, and knowing it they can decide whether to wait for next year. Mrs Oueidat asked about the difference between information and an invitation, and an invitation asks the reader to do something and information lets them decide whether to, and the second costs the applicant eleven seconds and the first costs them eleven weeks. Dr Qabbani asked whether that means she never encourages anybody, and it means she encourages when she means it and with a date on it, and the three applicants she genuinely encouraged this year got a round, a date and her name, and two of the three were funded. Mr Shihabi asked what happens if the condition is about the organisation and not about the world, and Mrs Oueidat said then say it, and it is the most useful condition there is and almost nobody writes it. Mr Tayara asked whether anybody ever does that, and one applicant did in July and his letter was better than hers. Mrs Tarabishi asked what happens if there is no condition at all, and Mrs Khoury said then there is no condition, and the letter says nothing about the future. And Mrs Rizk said the thing she will take away is the three letters, and that the man has not applied since, and the programme lost the strongest technical proposal in two rounds. And Mrs Ajouz said her representative asks her every month what would change the answer, and Mrs Oueidat said he is asking for a condition and there is one, which is that the stock list is set by the wholesaler and reviewed in January, a fact about a calendar that he cannot hurry, and that the monthly visit is the cost of never having told him what the calendar is.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The report ends on a file and the file is the teaching.** **Three letters of community ownership, obtained in five visits in February, which nobody has read since the refusal in March** — **and in the same file, a proposal recorded as the strongest in two rounds on technical soundness.** **Both documents are consequences of one sentence written because the letter felt cold.** **Ask the room what is in their own files.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **The manufacturable condition** → **six of eight; the letters arrive.**   **2** **_Should your circumstances change_** → **no circumstance named.**   **3** ⚠ **Encouragement with no date** → **it goes in because the letter feels cold.**   **4** **The organisational fact withheld as an admission** → **it is information.**   **5** ⚠ **A condition supplied where there is none** → **rows 5 of both cards.**   **6** **The condition stated and the real reason withheld** → **four of six, all known from the beginning.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **January: she wrote _if the evidence of community ownership were stronger_.** **February: three letters arrived, obtained in five visits.** **March: she refused the scheme because the programme had funded two schemes in that district** — **which she had known in January and had not written down.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **Can the applicant manufacture it?** **If they can, it is an instruction and they will carry it out; if they cannot, it is information and they can do arithmetic with it** — **and arithmetic about the future is the only thing a refusal has to offer.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **An applicant wrote to the secretariat about the allocation in July and copied her, and his letter was better than hers.** **The allocation has not changed and the question is now on a committee agenda where it had never been** — **and if it changes, it changes for every scheme in the governorate and not for his, which is the shape of 18.7 and should be named.**'));
