out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Rizk has to refuse a change proposed by the donor: they want the schemes scored on cost per household alone, and the reason they give is a good one, because nine criteria produce nine arguments and one figure produces a ranking. She is going to refuse it, and her first three drafts began by saying so, and all three were unsendable. Ms Huda asked what a first paragraph that says no produces, and Mrs Khoury said a reader who spends the rest of the document defending their proposal instead of reading yours, which is not a theory about feelings but what happens to attention. Mr Attar said so the first paragraph is the purpose, and their purpose, in their terms, and she has to mean it: four of her nine criteria are not comparable between districts and she has been scoring them as though they were, which is a concession and is true and which she had not put in writing before. Mrs Oueidat said and then the refusal, and then the one thing the change would do that defeats its own purpose, which is the whole architecture, because cost per household is not comparable between districts either, since the denominator is the beneficiary definition. Dr Qabbani said so their own purpose refuses it, and Mrs Khoury said their purpose refuses it, and that is the only refusal a proposal of this kind can survive. Mr Shihabi asked whether it has to end with a proposal of her own, and it does, and the proposal has to serve their purpose and not hers. Mr Tayara said she gives up something, and Mrs Oueidat said she gives up two of her nine criteria and the room should notice that it is not a gesture. Mrs Tarabishi asked what happens if their purpose is not a good one, and Mrs Khoury said then this is the wrong document. And Mrs Ajouz asked about the word but, and Mrs Rizk said it does not appear and finding that out took three drafts, and the donor\'s reply quoted her concession back at her as though it were their own sentence. Mrs Khoury also said that a refusal from your own preferences is an opinion against theirs, where a refusal from their purpose is arithmetic, and that a proposal whose purpose you reject is answered not with a counter-proposal but with a letter saying what you think the purpose should be, which is 22.1 and four units of work away. And Mrs Rizk said the version she sent has a full stop where each but had been.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last sentence of the report is the result and the room will treat it as a pleasantry.** **The donor\'s reply quoted her concession back at her as though it were their own sentence** — **which is what a refusal from the reader\'s own purpose produces: the reader adopts the sentence, and the writer gets the change she wanted and no credit for the paragraph.** **Ask the room whether that trade is acceptable, and let somebody say that it is not.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **The refusal in the first clause** → **nine of ten, on the first attempt.**   **2** **_While I understand the thinking_** → **a refusal in the clothes of agreement.**   **3** ⚠ **The concession that costs nothing** → **six of ten; had it been written down before?**   **4** **Three objections instead of one** → **the reader answers the easiest.**   **5** ⚠ **The counter-proposal that costs the writer nothing** → **identified by partners in under a minute.**   **6** **_But_ and _however_, and the audible pause** → **seven of ten; all struck.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **That the purpose is right and that the writer has been part of the problem it addresses**: four of her nine criteria are not comparable between districts and she has been scoring them as though they were, and ranking schemes on the total. **The concession is about herself and is the reason the rest of the proposal can be read.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **Cost per household is not comparable between districts either, because the denominator is the beneficiary definition at paragraph 2.4, which ends in _and others affected_.** **The figures: two schemes serving the same eleven villages reported two hundred and eighteen households and nine hundred, both within the definition** — **and a single figure would rank them four places apart on a number that measures nothing in common.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **Her proposal costs her two of the nine criteria, both of which she argued for in 2021, and the pass-or-fail treatment of technical soundness, which is the distinction she has been most attached to.** **It costs the secretariat a year** — **the single figure begins in the autumn round and not the spring one.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 6 · Write with help (sample)'));
