out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The second finding is about position and not about content, and it is the harder of the two to teach.** **The free sentence was in the letter, as the last line of a one-paragraph refusal, where it reads as consolation** — **and the applicant did not use it with his own board.** **Prove it with the room rather than asserting it: read the one-paragraph letter aloud, ending on the free sentence, and ask what the last line sounded like.** **Then read the four-line note with the same sentence first, and ask again.** ⚠ **Nothing in the words changes.** **The second version is evidence and the first is comfort, and the difference is the order** — **which is the only place in Book 2 where position alone carries a finding, and it should be named as such.**'));
