out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Khoury said there are three things and one of them is not a letter: two lines to the programme officer with the sentence she needed, one short note to the applicant with the free sentence at the top instead of the bottom, and a change to the standard refusal, which is the only one of the three worth anything next year. Mrs Rizk said what must not be said is that his board should have read the letter, and that is exactly it and it is true, which is the whole difficulty of the unit in one sentence: the free sentence was there, as the last line of a one-paragraph refusal, where it reads as consolation. Mrs Oueidat asked whether anybody is at fault, and Mr Attar said nobody, and this is the eighth time in Book 2: the writer gave one unremovable reason, the applicant took the letter to his board, the officer defended it with what she had, and the sentence that would have settled it was written down by the right person in the wrong document. Dr Qabbani said so the refusal was right, and Mrs Rizk said the refusal was right and the letter was incomplete, and she had thought those were the same thing, because a refusal has two readers and she had been writing for one of them. Mrs Khoury said that is the finding of the unit and it arrives in the last cycle: every refusal is defended by somebody, and the question to ask of a letter is not only whether it is right but whether the person who has to defend it can do so from the letter alone. Mr Shihabi asked what that sentence looks like, and it is the rule\'s purpose and it is one line, eighteen words, in her internal note since 2021 and in none of the twenty-seven refusals she wrote this year. Mr Tayara asked why it was never in the letter, and Mrs Oueidat said because it reads like an explanation and she had been taught that a refusal should not explain itself, and it is not an explanation: it is the rule\'s purpose. Mrs Tarabishi asked about the note to the applicant, and four lines, with the free sentence first. Mrs Ajouz asked whether the standard letter changes, and Mrs Khoury said it does, and that is the only part of this that outlives the three of them. And Mrs Rizk said the thing she will take away is the officer\'s own sentence: she could say what the rule was and could not say what it was for.']));
